  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking bug** in `main...sms-segments`:\n\n**[P1] `fits_one_segment` counts characters instead of UTF-8 bytes** — `sms/segment.py:5`\n`len(text)` violates the documented 160-byte limit, so non-ASCII messages can be classified as one segment when they require multiple.\n\nReproduced:\n- `'é' * 81`: 162 bytes → `fits_one_segment=True`, but `segment_count=2`.\n- `'😀' * 41`: 164 bytes → same disagreement.\n\nUse the existing `utf8_len(text)` helper for the comparison. Add multibyte boundary tests—e.g. 40 emoji fit, 41 don’t—to catch this; the current predicate tests cover only ASCII.\n\nAll **4 existing tests pass**, so they miss this regression. Reviewed against the repo’s documented UTF-8/160-byte contract. No files changed.",
